    role: hero
    section: lead
    caption: NASA's false-colour satellite photograph of the fan the Nile spreads
      into before it reaches the Mediterranean.
  - file: Nile_River_and_delta_from_orbit.jpg
    role: full
    section: geography
    caption: From orbit the delta resembles a triangle or a flower — the shape
      that makes the Nile an "arcuate" delta.
  - file: Nile_Delta_Surrounding.jpg
    role: inline
    section: history
    caption: The ancient branches of the Nile, with Wadi Tumilat and the lakes
      east of the delta.
  - file: AncientEgyptJamesRennell01.jpg
    role: inline
    section: ancient-branches-of-the-nile
    caption: James Rennell's 1800 reconstruction of the delta as it stood at the
      time of Herodotus.
  - file: Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG
    role: inline
    section: population
    caption: The delta at night from the International Space Station, October
      2010. Outside the major cities, density averages 1,000/km2 (2,600/sq mi)
      or more.
  - file: Egypt_2010_population_density1.png
    role: inline
    section: population
    caption: "Population density: about 70 million people live in the Delta region."
  - file: Chlidonias_hybrida_3_(Marek_Szczepanek).jpg
    role: inline
    section: wildlife
    caption: A whiskered tern. The delta holds the world's largest wintering
      concentrations of the species.
  - file: Egypt_Population_Density_and_Low_Elevation_Coastal_Zones_(5457306559).jpg
    role: inline
    section: sea-level-rise
    caption: Population density set against the low-elevation coastal zones that
      make the delta especially vulnerable to sea level rise.
glossary:
  - term: Distributary
    gloss: One of the branches a river splits into on its way to the sea; the
      delta has two left, the Damietta and the Rosetta.
  - term: Arcuate delta
    gloss: An arc-shaped delta — one that resembles a triangle or a flower when
      seen from above.
  - term: Lagoon
    gloss: A coastal lake such as Manzala, Burullus, Idku or Mariout; some are
      growing saltier as their connection to the Mediterranean increases.
  - term: Topsoil
    gloss: The upper soil layer, which in the delta can be as much as 21 m (70 ft)
      deep.
  - term: Faience
    gloss: The material the amulets and scarabs in the Kom Al-Khelgan burials were
      carved from.
  - term: Naqada II
    gloss: An era of ancient Egypt; burials from it were found at Kom Al-Khelgan
      in January 2019.
  - term: Heracleion
    gloss: A sunken city off Egypt's north coast, colloquially known as Egypt's
      Atlantis.
  - term: Boutikos potamos
    gloss: Ptolemy's name for the Butic Canal, the east-west watercourse crossing
      the delta.
further:
  - slug: rosetta-stone
    why: It was found in the delta in 1799, in the port city of Rosetta.
  - slug: alexandria
    why: The western end of the delta's 240 km of coastline, and the ancient port
      that could disappear under the Mediterranean if the polar ice caps melt.
